<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The three theme colours `styles.xml` references.

    This file did not exist, and the application was resolving all three from
    the defaults inside `@capacitor/android`, which are Material indigo
    `#3F51B5`, its dark variant `#303F9F`, and a magenta accent `#FF4081`. An
    application resource of the same name wins over a library one, so these
    four lines are all it takes to replace them.

    It matters because those values are not invisible. `colorPrimaryDark` paints
    the status bar before the web layer has loaded and had a chance to repaint
    it, `colorAccent` tints the text selection handles and the cursor inside
    every input in the WebView, and `colorPrimary` is what the launcher and the
    recents screen sample. A person would meet magenta selection handles inside
    a product that has had every warm and violet token deleted from its palette
    on the owner's explicit instruction.

    The values are the sampled brand anchors: base `#010118` for the darkest
    surface, mid `#000F98` for the primary, and glow `#0C39EF` for the accent
    that has to be visible against dark. `packages/design-tokens` remains the
    control surface for the product itself. These three are only the small
    amount of system-drawn chrome that never reaches the web layer, and they are
    written as literals because an Android resource cannot read a CSS token.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="colorPrimary">#000F98</color>
    <color name="colorPrimaryDark">#010118</color>
    <color name="colorAccent">#0C39EF</color>
</resources>
